kind how-do-i
title How do I show a terminal on a display that reports no EDID?
intro Without a udev daemon, vtium can match a display only by its monitor's EDID, its identity. A display that reports none can still show a terminal through a rule for every display. vtium-config does not pick such a display as itself, and says how to use All displays instead.
see heads-and-rules/show-a-terminal-on-a-display

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
device display HDMI-A-1
device keyboard 046d:c31c USB Keyboard

1. Go to the Flow tab.
2. Highlight HDMI-A-1.
3. Press Space to pick.
note vtium-config cannot pick the display as itself, and says how to show a terminal on it.
at the display picked as itself
check screen shows "reports no EDID"
check screen lacks "This path is complete"
4. Highlight Display.
5. Press Enter.
6. Highlight All displays.
7. Press Enter.
note PARTS now holds All displays, which matches every display, HDMI-A-1 included.
8. Press Space to pick.
9. Highlight USB Keyboard.
10. Press Space to pick.
at the path
check screen shows "This path is complete"
11. Press a to add path.
check screen lacks "This is not a valid rule"
12. Press s to save.
at the save
check draft display HDMI-A-1 reaches terminal-1
check draft input USB Keyboard reaches terminal-1
